      "content": "The variance route is a possibility, but the commission has been pretty strict lately about any \"encroachments\" that might infringe on the character of the existing neighborhood. If we can't get a variance, do you think there's a way to argue that these encroachments are \"grandfathered in\" so they don't trigger the new setback requirements for the whole site? I need to know if there's any legal precedent for treating existing boundary issues as static rather than something that needs to be corrected during reclassification.",
