    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. My main concern is how they'll view the actual physical nature of the encroachments. Some of them are small stuff, like old fence lines or low retaining walls that have been there for decades, while others go right up to the edge of the neighbor's driveway. If the commission sees these as \"intrusions\" that compromise the integrity of the new mixed-use zoning, I'm worried they'll reject the whole reclassification. How can I characterize these boundary overlaps so they don't seem like aggressive or problematic encroachments on the surrounding residential space?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
